    },
    {
      "claim": "L2 mostly repeats these positive values, but also shows that some high values are cirrhosis-dependent: pentazocine control F was 0.18 (C38) and meptazinol cirrhosis 27.9% was about a four-fold increase over controls (C24); pethidine normal F was 0.48 (C16) and paliperidone ER 'low' descriptions still correspond to 28% (C37).",
      "card_ids": ["C38","C24","C16","C37"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The query is a morphinan-like opioid with favorable absorption/solubility priors (logD 1.47, TPSA 73, MW 357) and no direct low-F measurement; the below-threshold control values come from different scaffolds and non-cirrhotic conditions and are not sufficient to establish F < 20% for the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C38","C24"]
    }
  ],
