      "direction": "contradictory",
      "decision_effect": "weakened",
      "card_ids": ["C38"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement for the query molecule is present in the supplied records.",
    "No healthy/non-cirrhotic morphinan context is available; the closest opioid contexts are cirrhosis-elevated or different scaffolds (pentazocine, pethidine, meptazinol, ciramadol).",
    "The extent of first-pass glucuronidation/sulfation of the query's phenol and hydroxyl groups is not quantified.",
    "Transferability of paliperidone, haloperidol, BI425809, and ACT-1004-1239 contexts is limited by chemotype mismatch."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Prediction remains high: all L1 gold-context records and most L2 context report F >= 20%, and no direct query-specific low-F evidence exists. L2 lowers confidence by revealing that some opioid controls have F < 20% in non-cirrhotic conditions, but those are different molecules/conditions and do not overturn the positive direction; uncertainty is captured as low confidence."
}

